-### Log Discovered Issues
-
-When bugs or tech debt are discovered during implementation:
+Run the full lifecycle per task yourself (the user only runs `/implement sprint-N`): health check → `br sync --import-only` → `br ready` → `br update <id> --status in_progress` → implement → `br close <id>` → `br sync --flush-only` at session end. Log discovered issues as they surface — this adds a `discovered-during:<parent-id>` label for traceability:
 
 ```bash
 .claude/scripts/beads/log-discovered-issue.sh "$CURRENT_TASK_ID" "Description of discovered issue" bug 2
 ```
 
-This creates a new issue with semantic label `discovered-during:<parent-id>` for traceability.
-
-### For each task:
-Implement to spec, following established project patterns (Karpathy principles govern style — they're in context every session). Tests: happy path + error conditions + edge cases, following existing test patterns; the runnable-check floor from CLAUDE.loa.md applies.
